The situations that count as formal non-compliance for a high-risk AI system are:
(a) the CE marking has been affixed in violation of Article 48 [AIA-Art83-1];
(b) the CE marking has not been affixed [AIA-Art83-1];
(c) the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 has not been drawn up [AIA-Art83-1];
(d) the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 has not been drawn up correctly [AIA-Art83-1];
(e) the registration in the EU database referred to in Article 71 has not been carried out [AIA-Art83-1];
(f) where applicable, no authorised representative has been appointed [AIA-Art83-1];
(g) technical documentation is not available [AIA-Art83-1].

The provided sources do not cover any additional situations of formal non-compliance beyond those listed.

Une autorité de surveillance du marché d'un État membre invite le fournisseur concerné à mettre un terme à la non-conformité lorsqu'elle fait l'une des constatations suivantes:
- le marquage CE a été apposé en violation de l'article 48 [AIA-Art83-1];
- le marquage CE n'a pas été apposé [AIA-Art83-1];
- la déclaration UE de conformité visée à l'article 47 n'a pas été établie [AIA-Art83-1];
- la déclaration UE de conformité visée à l'article 47 n'a pas été établie correctement [AIA-Art83-1];
- l'enregistrement dans la base de données de l'UE visée à l'article 71 n'a pas été effectué [AIA-Art83-1];
- le cas échéant, il n'a pas été désigné de mandataire [AIA-Art83-1];
- la documentation technique n'est pas disponible [AIA-Art83-1].

Union or Member State law to which the data controller or processor is subject may restrict by way of a legislative measure the scope of the obligations and rights provided for in Articles 12 to 22 and Article 34, as well as Article 5 (in so far as its provisions correspond to the rights and obligations provided for in Articles 12 to 22), when such a restriction respects the essence of the fundamental rights and freedoms and constitutes a necessary and proportionate measure in a democratic society to safeguard certain objectives [GDPR-Art23-1]. 

These objectives include:
- national security [GDPR-Art23-1];
- defence [GDPR-Art23-1];
- public security [GDPR-Art23-1];
- the prevention, investigation, detection, or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including safeguarding against and preventing threats to public security [GDPR-Art23-1];
- other important objectives of general public interest of the Union or of a Member State, such as important economic or financial interests (including monetary, budgetary, and taxation matters), public health, and social security [GDPR-Art23-1];
- the protection of judicial independence and judicial proceedings [GDPR-Art23-1];
- the prevention, investigation, detection, and prosecution of breaches of ethics for regulated professions [GDPR-Art23-1];
- monitoring, inspection, or regulatory functions connected, even occasionally, to the exercise of official authority in cases referred to in points (a) to (e) and (g) [GDPR-Art23-1];
- the protection of the data subject or the rights and freedoms of others [GDPR-Art23-1]; and
- the enforcement of civil law claims [GDPR-Art23-1].

Furthermore, any such legislative measure must contain specific provisions at least, where relevant, concerning:
- the purposes of the processing or categories of processing [GDPR-Art23-2];
- the categories of personal data [GDPR-Art23-2];
- the scope of the restrictions introduced [GDPR-Art23-2];
- the safeguards to prevent abuse or unlawful access or transfer [GDPR-Art23-2];
- the specification of the controller or categories of controllers [GDPR-Art23-2];
- the storage periods and applicable safeguards, taking into account the nature, scope, and purposes of the processing or categories of processing [GDPR-Art23-2];
- the risks to the rights and freedoms of data subjects [GDPR-Art23-2]; and
- the right of data subjects to be informed about the restriction, unless that may be prejudicial to the purpose of the restriction [GDPR-Art23-2].

The provided sources do not cover any other conditions or contexts under which data protection rights and obligations might be restricted beyond these legislative measures.

En particulier, toute mesure législative limitant la portée des obligations et des droits du RGPD contient des dispositions spécifiques relatives, au moins, le cas échéant:
- aux finalités du traitement ou des catégories de traitement [GDPR-Art23-2] ;
- aux catégories de données à caractère personnel [GDPR-Art23-2] ;
- à l'étendue des limitations introduites [GDPR-Art23-2] ;
- aux garanties destinées à prévenir les abus ou l'accès ou le transfert illicites [GDPR-Art23-2] ;
- à la détermination du responsable du traitement ou des catégories de responsables du traitement [GDPR-Art23-2] ;
- aux durées de conservation et aux garanties applicables, en tenant compte de la nature, de la portée et des finalités du traitement ou des catégories de traitement [GDPR-Art23-2] ;
- aux risques pour les droits et libertés des personnes concernées [GDPR-Art23-2] ; et
- au droit des personnes concernées d'être informées de la limitation, à moins que cela risque de nuire à la finalité de la limitation [GDPR-Art23-2].
